                                                             L1_paramdef.h 
This header file defines the gNB L1 configuration schema by declaring string keys (CONFIG_STRING_*), a parameter descriptor table (L1PARAMS_DESC) 
with types and default values and numeric index macros for each option. 
At runtime the option parser uses this table to register and provide parsed values (accessed by those indices) that control L1 behavior like 
network addresses, DTX thresholds, OFDM timing, and LDPC iteration limits.

  Key parameters are :
  1.num_cc(CONFIG_STRING_L1_CC,default 1) stands for the number of component carriers. By increasing num_cc raises peak throughput 
  but also increases CPU load, memory use, scheduling complexity and RF/resource management overhead.Crutial for the performance is to set the
  value in such way which would not overload the hardware. 

  2.max_ldpc_iterations(CONFIG_STRING_L1_MAX_LDPC_ITERATIONS,default 5) controls the upper limit on LDPC decoder iterations.By regulating the 
  parameter the error rate(BLER) can be controlled which will result in more CPU usage. 

  3.ofdm_offset_divisor(CONFIG_STRING_L1_OFDM_OFFSET_DIVISOR,default 8) servers for control of the OFDM timing/offset scalling which is used by PHY.

  4.Thread-pool(CONFIG_STRING_L1_THREAD_POOL_SIZE entry) sets the number of threads available for L1 tasks.

  5.DTX thresholds (PUCCH0, PRACH, PUSCH) control decision t 

  6. transport preference / local remote addresses and ports (tr_n_preference, local_n_address, remote_n_address, local_n_portc/portd)
